> Inspect the native model architecture

This separate trace calls the same canonical source graph and uses its original hidden/input/action sizes. Twin-critic and stochastic methods show one representative critic and a mean action for readability; the full experiment retains all critics and sampled actions. The trace initializes separate stores and does not change fitting.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/d4pg_network.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){namespace n=dm::nn;namespace m=n::models;std::filesystem::create_directories("build");n::ParameterStore p(0),q(1);std::vector<float>atoms(51);for(int i=0;i<51;++i)atoms[i]=-1000+i*20;auto support=n::from_vector(atoms);n::Module network([&](const n::Tensor& x){auto a=m::DeterministicActor(p,"pi",x,1,128);return m::DistributionalActionCritic(q,x,a,128,support).q;},"d4pg source model");n::ModelPlotOptions options;options.detail=n::ModelPlotDetail::Blocks;options.sizing.minimum_extent=2;options.sizing.max_planes=2;network.plot(n::zeros({1,3}),options).save_svg("build/d4pg_network.svg");}
