> Actual eval diagnostics

These values come from the preserved source run above. Evaluation calls remain in their original order and may include different final policies, such as SAC mean versus sampled actions. One point does not establish a learning trend. The hybrid histogram retains raw source counts; task rewards and intrinsic bonuses are separate quantities.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/d4pg_eval.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){auto archive=dm::nn::load_npz("build/d4pg_source.npz");auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();bool calls=std::any_of(archive.begin(),archive.end(),[](const auto& p){return p.first=="eval_call";});for(const auto&[key,t]:archive){if(calls?key!="eval_call":!key.starts_with("eval_"))continue;auto y=t.to_vector<double>();std::vector<double>x(y.size());std::iota(x.begin(),x.end(),1.);plot.lines(x,y,key,{37,99,235}).points(x,y,key+" points",{37,99,235},5);}plot.title("d4pg actual eval diagnostics").x_label("Existing source evaluation call").y_label("Task return").size(1100,600).save_svg("build/d4pg_eval.svg");}
